    "text": "On September 30, 2026, a Flydubai flight (FZ1073) traveling from Dubai to Tel Aviv was diverted to Tabuk airport in Saudi Arabia following a midair altercation in the cockpit. According to reports, an unnamed co-pilot allegedly stabbed the captain, an Indian national identified as Smit Machchhar, and attempted to take control of the aircraft. The plane reportedly plunged more than 17,000 feet during the incident, causing the rudder to be ripped off. Passengers and crew members were able to overpower the attacker and stabilize the plane. Captain Machchhar was reported to be in stable condition in a hospital. The United Arab Emirates’ chief prosecutor, Hamad Saif Al Shamsi, has launched an investigation to determine if the incident was linked to terrorist activity, intent, or prior planning. Netanyahu stated that the suspect is being investigated in Saudi Arabia and is expected to be transferred to the UAE. While Netanyahu claimed the co-pilot had undergone 'Islamist radical indoctrination' and suggested potential Iranian involvement, he also noted it was too early to establish a specific motive or confirm Iran's role. The Israeli foreign ministry stated that passengers on the aircraft included citizens from Israel, India, and the UAE."
